  'The primary distinction lies in shareholder count. A Free Zone Establishment (FZE) is incorporated with a single shareholder (which can be an individual person or a corporate entity). A Free Zone Company (FZC or FZ-LLC) accommodates two or more shareholders (up to 50 in many jurisdictions). Both legal structures provide limited liability protection, safeguarding personal assets to the extent of contributed share capital.': 'The primary distinction lies in shareholder count. A Free Zone Establishment (FZE) is incorporated with a single shareholder (which can be an individual person or a corporate entity). A Free Zone Company (FZC or FZ-LLC) accommodates two or more shareholders (up to 50 in many jurisdictions). Both legal structures provide limited liability protection, safeguarding personal assets to the extent of contributed share capital.',
