  'Yes, but subject to specific commercial regulations. Free zone entities can freely conduct business with other free zones and international markets. For selling goods directly into the UAE mainland, a free zone company can either appoint a licensed mainland distributor/agent, set up a mainland LLC branch office, or pay the standard 5% customs duty upon clearing goods through UAE customs. For professional and consulting services, free zone firms can deliver advisory services to mainland corporate clients provided work is primarily executed from the free zone or under proper contracting agreements.': 'Yes, but subject to specific commercial regulations. Free zone entities can freely conduct business with other free zones and international markets. For selling goods directly into the UAE mainland, a free zone company can either appoint a licensed mainland distributor/agent, set up a mainland LLC branch office, or pay the standard 5% customs duty upon clearing goods through UAE customs. For professional and consulting services, free zone firms can deliver advisory services to mainland corporate clients provided work is primarily executed from the free zone or under proper contracting agreements.',
  'Yes. Free zone companies are fully eligible to apply for corporate bank accounts with leading UAE commercial banks (such as Emirates NBD, Mashreq, Abu Dhabi Commercial Bank, Dubai Islamic Bank, and Wio Bank). Approval is subject to the bank’s stringent Know-Your-Customer (KYC) and Anti-Money Laundering (AML) due diligence, which evaluates shareholder profiles, legitimate source of funds, business plans, commercial contracts, and verified company substance in the UAE.': 'Yes. Free zone companies are fully eligible to apply for corporate bank accounts with leading UAE commercial banks (such as Emirates NBD, Mashreq, Abu Dhabi Commercial Bank, Dubai Islamic Bank, and Wio Bank). Approval is subject to the bank’s stringent Know-Your-Customer (KYC) and Anti-Money Laundering (AML) due diligence, which evaluates shareholder profiles, legitimate source of funds, business plans, commercial contracts, and verified company substance in the UAE.',
  'Yes. Free zones have always guaranteed 100% foreign ownership with zero requirement for a local UAE national shareholder or local service agent. Foreign investors maintain complete control over company shares, operational decisions, and profit repatriation without currency exchange restrictions.': 'Yes. Free zones have always guaranteed 100% foreign ownership with zero requirement for a local UAE national shareholder or local service agent. Foreign investors maintain complete control over company shares, operational decisions, and profit repatriation without currency exchange restrictions.',
